# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in the value(s) below.
#
# Formspree form ID — the contact form posts submissions here, which Formspree
# forwards to your inbox. Create a free form at https://formspree.io, then copy
# the ID from the form's endpoint URL (https://formspree.io/f/XXXXXXXX -> XXXXXXXX).
#
# For local dev: put it in a ".env" file (gitignored).
# For production (AWS Amplify): add it as a build environment variable in the
# Amplify console (App settings -> Environment variables) with the same name.
#
# Leaving this unset is fine: the ID is public (it is the POST endpoint), so the
# component carries a hardcoded default and the form still works.
VITE_FORMSPREE_ID=

# Formspree form ID for the field-notes subscribe box, which is a DIFFERENT
# list from the contact form and should be a different form.
#
# Unset, SubscribeCard falls back to the contact form's ID and both streams pile
# into one place, separated only by the `_subject` line Formspree stamps on the
# email. That is survivable in an inbox and a real problem the day the list is
# exported: a bulk import would sweep up everyone who ever sent a project
# inquiry and put them on a mailing list they never joined. Create a second free
# form at https://formspree.io, set it here and in the Amplify console, and the
# two are separate from that point on.
VITE_FORMSPREE_NOTES_ID=
